        "original_id": "bfbc4c4a-fe09-5178-8066-e3ecc2dfe5e7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rashi Bunny, Arvind Gaur, Bhisham Sahni, Manjula Padmanabhan, Antoine de Saint-Exupéry, Rahul Gandhi\n- Works: Madhavi, Hidden Fires, The Little Prince\n- Organizations: Sahara India Group\n- Topics: Indian theatre, cinema, theatre workshops\n\nFacts:\n- Antoine de Saint-Exupéry first published The Little Prince in 1943.\n- The Little Prince is a novella and the most famous work of Antoine de Saint-Exupéry.\n- Rashi Bunny is an Indian theatre and cinema actress.\n- Rashi Bunny performed in Bhisham Sahni's Madhavi, Manjula Padmanabhan's Hidden Fires, and Antoine de Saint-Exupéry's The Little Prince with director Arvind Gaur.\n- Sahara India Group selected Rashi Bunny as one of the 50 Icons: Emerging personality of India with Rahul Gandhi.\n- Rashi Bunny is also known for the I Have a Dream theatre workshop for self-exploration and creative expression.",
